      "description": "Association provides only 96-bit security",
      "detail": "Component strengths: encryption 128 bits, prf 96 bits, integrity 96 bits, key_exchange 112 bits. The association is bounded by its prf at 96 bits, which is graded 'deprecated'. A strong cipher does not compensate for a weak key exchange: an attacker who recovers the session key never has to attack the cipher at all.",
      "recommendation": "Raise the prf to at least the 128-bit level. The whole suite should be re-specified together rather than patched component by component.",
